======================================================================================
S726 — Erdos 61: the chromatic-4 targets are a Mycielski tower from C_5 (= Paley P_5, S725)
======================================================================================

61 (OPEN): G1,G2 with chi=aleph_1 => common subgraph G with chi(G)=4 (or aleph_0)?
Erdos remark: probably every aleph_1-chromatic graph contains EVERY chromatic-4 LARGE-GIRTH
graph => any two share one => 61 reduces to UNAVOIDABILITY of chromatic-4-large-girth graphs.

  level 0: C_5 (=Paley P_5, S725 seed)  |V|= 5  chi=3  girth=5  alpha=2  #ind-sets=11  I(G,2)-coeff_2=5
  level 1: M(C_5)=Grotzsch              |V|=11  chi=4  girth=4  alpha=5  #ind-sets=103  I(G,2)-coeff_2=35
  level 2: M^2(C_5)                     |V|=23  chi=5  girth=4  alpha=11  #ind-sets=7407  I(G,2)-coeff_2=182

  => the Mycielski tower from C_5 climbs chi = 3,4,5,... (additive ladder), triangle-free
     preserved (girth >=4). LEVEL 1 = Grotzsch = the canonical chromatic-4 (girth-4) graph =
     the finite SEED of 61's unavoidable target. The tower is a graph TRANSFER (S720/721).

THE REDUCTION + HEURISTIC (creative, leveraging S725):
  - 61's common-subgraph question <= UNAVOIDABILITY: every aleph_1-chromatic graph contains
    every chromatic-4-large-girth graph (then two such graphs share one).
  - the targets form a RECURSIVE TOWER from C_5 (Mycielski for girth 4; high-girth needs
    Ramanujan/probabilistic towers -- the hard 'large girth' case).
  - S725 RENORMALIZATION reading: aleph_1 (uncountable = a 'limit/fixed point') forces the
    whole finite obstruction tower, as limit ordinals restore partition relations (Chang).
    The finite levels are 'hot' (avoidable individually); the uncountable limit is the 'cold
    fixed point' that cannot avoid the tower -- the renormalization that should force the target.
  - COMMON-subgraph as INTERSECTION: G1 cap G2 contains the tower iff BOTH contain it; the
    unavoidability makes the intersection nonempty at chromatic-4. (THM-209 independence tracks
    the shared level.)
  - GIRTH is the obstruction (as in S722/S723: large girth = locally tree/ultrametric, the S725
    laminar structure). chi-4 + large girth = a high-temperature target; aleph_1 = the limit
    forcing it. The program: prove unavoidability of the Mycielski/high-girth tower in
    aleph_1-chromatic graphs via the renormalization/elementary-submodel-tower method.
